      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "Statistical interface:\n  Y_ij = X_ij'beta + alpha_i + psi_j + u_i' Lambda v_j + error_ij,\n  rank(Lambda)=r.\n\nKey design choice:\n  alpha_i and psi_j remain unrestricted. The rank restriction applies to h_ij.\n\nWhy this is the right nesting direction:\n  AKM is nested by setting Lambda=0.\n  BLM-type grouped mean layers imply a low-rank double-demeaned interaction after lifting type cells.\n  Kline-style edge restrictions are diagnostics on differences, not a complete level model unless augmented.",
